1
00:00:00,005 --> 00:00:04,369
[The day before the Tutu-Tuesla launch]

2
00:00:13,166 --> 00:00:16,957
It's finally here. Tomorrow
is your world debut, huh?

3
00:00:16,957 --> 00:00:20,666
Everyone will definitely
fall in love with Tuesla.

4
00:00:21,281 --> 00:00:24,977
<i>♪ Tu! Tu! Tuesla! Tutu-Tuesla! ♪</i>

5
00:00:24,977 --> 00:00:28,766
<i>♪ Tu! Tu! Tuesla! Tutu-Tuesla! ♪</i>

6
00:00:30,866 --> 00:00:33,066
<i>So cute.</i>

7
00:00:34,133 --> 00:00:37,757
- <i>♪ Tuesla, Tuesla, Tu... ♪</i>
- What's this?

8
00:00:37,757 --> 00:00:39,645
Is something wrong?

9
00:00:40,257 --> 00:00:42,237
No, nothing...

10
00:00:47,577 --> 00:00:50,805
- Static electricity!
- Huh?

11
00:00:50,805 --> 00:00:52,921
Didn't you feel that just now? Like, zap!

12
00:00:52,921 --> 00:00:54,133
No, not at all.

13
00:00:54,133 --> 00:00:56,781
- What?
- I didn't feel anything.

14
00:00:56,781 --> 00:00:58,669
So it was just me?

15
00:00:58,669 --> 00:01:02,257
- I was the only one who got shocked?
- Come on. Let's get these lined up.

16
00:01:02,257 --> 00:01:05,005
<i>♪ Tu! Tu! Tutu-Tuesla! Tutu... ♪</i>

17
00:01:05,005 --> 00:01:06,801
[Kitchen Sakoda]
Wow, that's amazing,

18
00:01:06,801 --> 00:01:08,413
[Reserved Today]
Ms. Kusakabe.

19
00:01:08,413 --> 00:01:10,609
To be able to have it placed
in such a famous place.

20
00:01:10,609 --> 00:01:13,373
- Really impressive.
- Oh, it's nothing special.

21
00:01:13,373 --> 00:01:15,953
For Tuesla, I'll use all
my connections and experience.

22
00:01:15,953 --> 00:01:17,781
I'll put them to full use.

23
00:01:17,781 --> 00:01:22,505
And so, to Tuesla's debut! Cheers!

24
00:01:22,505 --> 00:01:26,013
- Tu-tu-tu!
- Tu-tu-tu!

25
00:01:28,753 --> 00:01:31,400
- What's wrong?
- Nothing.

26
00:01:32,081 --> 00:01:33,925
What's this?

27
00:01:34,845 --> 00:01:38,833
Sorry I couldn't help with the delivery.
My back is a bit...

28
00:01:39,465 --> 00:01:41,393
You have back problems too?

29
00:01:41,393 --> 00:01:44,829
- Yes, that's right.
- Me too.

30
00:01:44,829 --> 00:01:47,345
If you'd like, I found a good chiropractor.

31
00:01:47,345 --> 00:01:48,437
Would you like me to introduce you?

32
00:01:48,437 --> 00:01:50,329
Really? That would be great!

33
00:01:50,329 --> 00:01:54,485
- Let's definitely go together.
- So cute. Tuesla.

34
00:01:54,485 --> 00:01:58,266
- As for that, it's been 20 years already...
- That's why...

35
00:01:58,266 --> 00:02:00,941
Tuesla is a genius!

36
00:02:00,941 --> 00:02:03,673
A genius of cuteness! Genius!

37
00:02:03,673 --> 00:02:05,385
You've had way too much to drink!

38
00:02:05,385 --> 00:02:09,185
No more alcohol. Have some tea.

39
00:02:09,185 --> 00:02:11,073
[Barley tea]
Mugi...

40
00:02:11,073 --> 00:02:15,209
Mugi... Why?

41
00:02:15,209 --> 00:02:18,721
- We were in love!
- Come on. Let's wrap this up. Okay?

42
00:02:18,721 --> 00:02:21,669
How are you feeling, Ms. Kusakabe?
Can you stand?

43
00:02:22,605 --> 00:02:25,641
Oh, no, no, no, no...

44
00:02:25,641 --> 00:02:27,313
Excuse me, we'll be leaving now.

45
00:02:27,313 --> 00:02:28,861
- Ow, ow, ow!
- You're totally wasted.

46
00:02:28,861 --> 00:02:30,197
- Ow!
- Come on, get on!

47
00:02:30,197 --> 00:02:32,981
- Take care!
- No! Anna Kusakabe can do it!

48
00:02:32,981 --> 00:02:34,249
- Come on, get on! Hurry...
- Please let me do it!

49
00:02:34,249 --> 00:02:36,329
I can still do it! I can!

50
00:02:36,329 --> 00:02:37,409
- Thank you in advance.
- Come on, come on.

51
00:02:37,409 --> 00:02:38,413
- Fine, fine, fine.
- Static electricity.

52
00:02:38,413 --> 00:02:40,537
- Come on! Fine, fine.
- Please take care of me!

53
00:02:40,537 --> 00:02:42,401
Yes, yes, yes, get on! Come on, come on.

54
00:02:42,401 --> 00:02:44,029
- Here, take this.
- Mugi...

55
00:02:44,029 --> 00:02:46,408
- Yes, get on! Fine, fine.
- Mugi...

56
00:02:46,408 --> 00:02:48,428
[Surcharge]

57
00:02:55,173 --> 00:02:59,669
Well, earlier, you said you knew
a good chiropractor, right?

58
00:02:59,669 --> 00:03:02,353
My chest has been hurting a bit lately.

59
00:03:02,353 --> 00:03:04,545
What kind of pain?

60
00:03:04,545 --> 00:03:06,821
Well, it's like...

61
00:03:06,821 --> 00:03:10,445
Like a sharp prick or throbbing.

62
00:03:10,445 --> 00:03:12,269
I see.

63
00:03:12,269 --> 00:03:16,613
And also a tingling, kind of numb feeling.

64
00:03:16,613 --> 00:03:20,849
I've experienced that too.

65
00:03:21,629 --> 00:03:25,200
Huh? Is it some kind of illness?

66
00:03:27,825 --> 00:03:29,700
Well, it's...

67
00:03:30,757 --> 00:03:32,737
It's what?

68
00:03:33,821 --> 00:03:37,597
Intercostal neuralgia.

69
00:03:37,597 --> 00:03:40,245
Intercostal neuralgia?

70
00:03:40,245 --> 00:03:42,117
Really? How do you know?

71
00:03:42,117 --> 00:03:45,893
I didn't live this long for nothing.

72
00:03:45,893 --> 00:03:49,513
I see. Intercostal neuralgia.

73
00:03:49,513 --> 00:03:52,866
Now that I know that, I feel better. Thanks.

74
00:03:52,866 --> 00:03:54,757
[Character Park]

75
00:03:54,757 --> 00:03:57,801
[Tutu-Tuesla Launch Day]
Welcome!

76
00:03:57,801 --> 00:04:00,700
Come on, come on,
step right up and take a look!

77
00:04:00,700 --> 00:04:02,949
Cuteness explosion, peak freshness!

78
00:04:02,949 --> 00:04:06,161
On sale today, it's Tutu-Tuesla!

79
00:04:06,161 --> 00:04:08,833
- Yes, yes! Take a look, take a look!
- A greengrocer?

80
00:04:15,133 --> 00:04:17,625
Wait, wait, wait! No one's coming at all!

81
00:04:17,625 --> 00:04:19,693
That's strange.

82
00:04:21,666 --> 00:04:25,466
Harsh Review Molco goes on sale at noon!

83
00:04:25,466 --> 00:04:29,125
Please don't push!
We're handing out numbered tickets!

84
00:04:29,125 --> 00:04:32,349
On sale today! Harsh Review Molco!

85
00:04:32,349 --> 00:04:34,693
Harsh Review Molco?

86
00:04:34,693 --> 00:04:36,581
Omishima.

87
00:04:36,581 --> 00:04:39,401
He deliberately launched it
on the same day as our Tuesla launch!

88
00:04:39,401 --> 00:04:41,409
Go, Harsh Review Molco.

89
00:04:41,409 --> 00:04:44,093
Wipe out Tuesla!

90
00:04:52,897 --> 00:04:56,133
Saying this or that, he must
have made someone do this.

91
00:04:56,133 --> 00:04:57,833
That can't be.

92
00:04:58,885 --> 00:05:02,200
There's no way the president would do that.

93
00:05:03,037 --> 00:05:06,521
Ah, you're from Merry... Well...

94
00:05:06,521 --> 00:05:08,705
My surname is Sasaoka.

95
00:05:08,705 --> 00:05:11,793
I came to check on the sales of
Harsh Review Molco,

96
00:05:11,793 --> 00:05:13,541
but it's already sold out.

97
00:05:13,541 --> 00:05:17,965
It went on sale at noon...
and sold out in three minutes?

98
00:05:17,965 --> 00:05:19,917
Restroom.

99
00:05:22,745 --> 00:05:24,917
It's not selling, is it?

100
00:05:25,845 --> 00:05:28,417
No, I mean, it's still early.

101
00:05:28,417 --> 00:05:30,689
It's the type to catch on later on.

102
00:05:30,689 --> 00:05:32,633
It's a late bloomer.

103
00:05:32,633 --> 00:05:35,529
Why do you only have plushies?

104
00:05:35,529 --> 00:05:38,393
As a result of emphasizing
the concept of Just Support,

105
00:05:38,393 --> 00:05:41,085
we decided that going all-in on plushies
would be the best approach.

106
00:05:41,085 --> 00:05:43,093
What's this character's background?

107
00:05:43,093 --> 00:05:46,029
He comes from a planet called Tutu Planet

108
00:05:46,029 --> 00:05:48,425
and is always alone, living in a burrow.

109
00:05:48,425 --> 00:05:50,493
But then one day, when he came to Earth,

110
00:05:50,493 --> 00:05:53,000
he saw a ballet tutu and thought,
"Ah! That's like mine..."

111
00:05:53,000 --> 00:05:57,409
Wouldn't it be better to push that story
and worldview more to the forefront?

112
00:05:57,409 --> 00:05:59,961
Without having to explain
to each customer individually,

113
00:05:59,961 --> 00:06:02,300
by means of conveying it clearly at a glance.

114
00:06:03,633 --> 00:06:05,541
I see.

115
00:06:22,549 --> 00:06:24,485
I'll buy this.

116
00:06:25,153 --> 00:06:26,993
You'll buy it?

117
00:06:26,993 --> 00:06:28,057
Do you like it?

118
00:06:28,057 --> 00:06:31,966
I'm only purchasing it to
research a competitor's product.

119
00:06:32,625 --> 00:06:34,600
Thank you very much.

120
00:06:36,773 --> 00:06:39,565
In the end, we only sold one.

121
00:06:39,565 --> 00:06:43,589
But my question is,
why did you sell it to Ms. Sasaoka?

122
00:06:43,589 --> 00:06:46,266
Well, if someone wants to buy something,
you sell it to them, right?

123
00:06:46,266 --> 00:06:49,146
She betrays people without batting an eye.

124
00:06:49,146 --> 00:06:52,281
Cold-blooded and ruthless enough
to make a spy pale.

125
00:06:52,281 --> 00:06:54,266
She tosses people aside like nothing.

126
00:06:54,869 --> 00:06:56,866
Cold-blooded?

127
00:06:56,866 --> 00:06:59,366
Really?

128
00:07:00,065 --> 00:07:02,573
That's not the impression I got from her.

129
00:07:02,573 --> 00:07:05,181
The points she mentioned made sense to me.

130
00:07:05,181 --> 00:07:08,566
No, no, no! You're being fooled.
You're being fooled.

131
00:07:16,361 --> 00:07:18,366
Tutu-Tuesla.

132
00:07:22,085 --> 00:07:24,966
Throwing people around is crazy,
normally speaking.

133
00:07:29,433 --> 00:07:31,409
Well... can I help you?

134
00:07:31,409 --> 00:07:36,697
My surname is Yagi.
I'm from Savannah Central Bank.

135
00:07:36,697 --> 00:07:39,961
[Savannah Central Bank, Noritaka Yagi]
Savannah Central Bank?

136
00:07:39,961 --> 00:07:42,557
About the product you are selling...

137
00:07:44,005 --> 00:07:48,541
We would like you
to stop selling Tutu-Tuesla.

138
00:07:48,541 --> 00:07:49,885
- Huh?
- What?

139
00:07:49,885 --> 00:07:54,100
That character is a copy of
our bank's mascot,

140
00:07:55,673 --> 00:07:57,400
isn't it?

141
00:07:59,269 --> 00:08:01,000
- What?
- What?

142
00:08:08,397 --> 00:08:11,921
[Episode 5]

143
00:08:11,921 --> 00:08:16,293
This is the mascot character for
Savannah Central Bank.

144
00:08:16,293 --> 00:08:18,357
Its name is Hi, Ena.

145
00:08:18,357 --> 00:08:20,609
- Hi?
- Ena?

146
00:08:20,609 --> 00:08:23,437
It's modeled after a hyena,

147
00:08:23,437 --> 00:08:25,757
which lives robustly and shrewdly
in the savannah.

148
00:08:25,757 --> 00:08:29,849
It appears in our company brochures
and on our website.

149
00:08:31,769 --> 00:08:38,673
Your Tutu-Tuesla is clearly
a rip-off of our Hi, Ena.

150
00:08:38,673 --> 00:08:41,665
There's no way it's a rip-off.
We didn't even know about this.

151
00:08:41,665 --> 00:08:45,081
Tuesla was created
by my overwhelming sense of style.

152
00:08:45,081 --> 00:08:46,801
That's how it was born.

153
00:08:46,801 --> 00:08:50,057
But please look.

154
00:08:50,057 --> 00:08:54,309
Being a hyena and having a cloth
wrapped around the waist.

155
00:08:54,309 --> 00:08:57,033
Don't you think these two points
are quite similar?

156
00:08:57,033 --> 00:08:59,533
Huh? Do you think so?

157
00:08:59,533 --> 00:09:01,213
Not at all.

158
00:09:01,213 --> 00:09:05,357
In any case, if you don't stop selling it,

159
00:09:05,357 --> 00:09:08,253
we will have to consider legal action.

160
00:09:08,253 --> 00:09:10,085
Legal action?

161
00:09:10,085 --> 00:09:13,149
Stop selling it immediately.

162
00:09:15,889 --> 00:09:17,765
This is bad. This is bad.

163
00:09:17,765 --> 00:09:20,393
A lawsuit is bad! A lawsuit is bad!

164
00:09:20,393 --> 00:09:22,729
Look, it's not similar at all.

165
00:09:22,729 --> 00:09:24,861
It's fine. We didn't copy it.

166
00:09:24,861 --> 00:09:25,997
We'll think of a response.

167
00:09:25,997 --> 00:09:29,413
For now, let's focus on selling Tuesla.

168
00:09:33,413 --> 00:09:35,957
You're withdrawing it?
That would put us in a tough spot.

169
00:09:35,957 --> 00:09:39,037
We can't keep selling a product
that's been called a rip-off.

170
00:09:39,037 --> 00:09:41,597
- So, I'm sorry, but...
- I told you, it's not a rip-off!

171
00:09:41,597 --> 00:09:43,173
It's genuinely my creation.

172
00:09:43,173 --> 00:09:47,549
But now that we've heard such rumors,
we can't continue selling it like this.

173
00:09:47,549 --> 00:09:49,877
That would put our credibility at risk.

174
00:09:58,521 --> 00:10:02,933
Sorry, sorry.

175
00:10:12,257 --> 00:10:14,300
[Free Consultations Available]
Sorry.

176
00:10:16,505 --> 00:10:19,321
That was tough. Really tough.

177
00:10:19,321 --> 00:10:21,101
That hurts!

178
00:10:21,101 --> 00:10:22,701
I'm back.

179
00:10:22,701 --> 00:10:25,069
Where did you go?

180
00:10:25,069 --> 00:10:26,766
It was really tough doing that
on my own, you know.

181
00:10:26,766 --> 00:10:30,877
Sorry, sorry. But when you hear this,
you'll definitely thank me.

182
00:10:30,877 --> 00:10:33,453
I've brought a savior.

183
00:10:33,453 --> 00:10:34,453
A savior?

184
00:10:34,453 --> 00:10:37,593
That savannah goat
or alpaca or whatever it is,

185
00:10:37,593 --> 00:10:41,341
if they're up for it, we'll do it too,
you know? We'll do it!

186
00:10:41,341 --> 00:10:43,713
An eye for an eye, a hyena for a hyena.

187
00:10:43,713 --> 00:10:46,341
For a lawsuit, a lawyer!

188
00:10:46,341 --> 00:10:49,585
- A lawyer?
- Don't underestimate my connections.

189
00:10:49,585 --> 00:10:52,127
Please, Mr. Lawyer! Come on!

190
00:11:03,269 --> 00:11:06,241
- Mugi.
- Mugi?

191
00:11:06,241 --> 00:11:09,465
- Anna.
- Anna?

192
00:11:10,585 --> 00:11:12,389
What's going on?

193
00:11:13,613 --> 00:11:20,269
He... Mugi is my ex-boyfriend.

194
00:11:22,689 --> 00:11:24,200
Ex-boyfriend?

195
00:11:24,200 --> 00:11:27,466
Wait, wait! I heard there is
a rip-off scandal. Are you okay...

196
00:11:30,277 --> 00:11:32,113
What's with this atmosphere?

197
00:11:34,661 --> 00:11:37,066
Well, so in other words,

198
00:11:37,685 --> 00:11:39,967
the lawyer you hired
to clear us of the allegation

199
00:11:39,967 --> 00:11:41,800
of ripping off someone else's character

200
00:11:42,409 --> 00:11:45,800
is Ms. Kusakabe's ex-boyfriend?

201
00:11:50,505 --> 00:11:55,329
Oh... Where did you two meet?

202
00:11:55,329 --> 00:12:00,241
Ah... Well, at the town's
free legal consultation office.

203
00:12:00,241 --> 00:12:04,965
Well, as far as I'm concerned,
I only intended to consult,

204
00:12:04,965 --> 00:12:09,645
but this person was in trouble
and insisted I come,

205
00:12:09,645 --> 00:12:13,253
saying he'd pay the legal fees,
and even half-forcing me...

206
00:12:13,253 --> 00:12:15,765
Is that true, Mr. Seo? Huh?

207
00:12:15,765 --> 00:12:18,605
- Mumble mutter...
- This is such a pain!

208
00:12:18,605 --> 00:12:20,525
Talk it out yourselves.

209
00:12:20,525 --> 00:12:25,785
Well... but copyright law
isn't really my specialty.

210
00:12:25,785 --> 00:12:29,689
Oh, it's not your specialty?

211
00:12:29,689 --> 00:12:32,753
Then please go home.

212
00:12:32,753 --> 00:12:39,553
But if Anna is in trouble,
I want to help in some way...

213
00:12:39,553 --> 00:12:42,586
I mean, I want to do what I can.

214
00:12:45,193 --> 00:12:48,400
- Mugi.
- Anna.

215
00:12:54,505 --> 00:12:58,001
Alright then, I'll look into it on my end.

216
00:12:58,001 --> 00:13:00,853
Okay. Thank you.

217
00:13:09,949 --> 00:13:12,021
I've met someone I like.

218
00:13:13,465 --> 00:13:15,345
Hello.

219
00:13:17,753 --> 00:13:21,285
- You're slow. Get on. Hurry.
- Oh, sorry.

220
00:13:21,285 --> 00:13:23,301
- See you.
- Okay.

221
00:13:23,301 --> 00:13:25,749
- I'll leave you behind.
- Alright, sorry.

222
00:13:27,697 --> 00:13:30,409
- You're slow.
- Sorry.

223
00:13:30,409 --> 00:13:35,977
<i>♪ The ex-boyfriend who dumped me ♪</i>

224
00:13:35,977 --> 00:13:41,689
<i>♪ Was being henpecked by his girlfriend ♪</i>

225
00:13:41,689 --> 00:13:46,433
<i>♪ I didn't want to see that ♪</i>

226
00:13:47,052 --> 00:13:48,752
<i>♪ Mu... ♪</i>

227
00:13:50,997 --> 00:13:52,929
Mugi.

228
00:14:01,329 --> 00:14:03,709
Please, let us sell Tuesla here.

229
00:14:03,709 --> 00:14:06,689
A product with allegations
of being a rip-off is a bit...

230
00:14:06,689 --> 00:14:09,233
- That's completely groundless.
- Sorry.

231
00:14:09,233 --> 00:14:10,793
- Please.
- Sorry.

232
00:14:10,793 --> 00:14:12,237
I'm sorry.

233
00:14:12,237 --> 00:14:15,157
Please, just hear us out.

234
00:14:16,293 --> 00:14:18,133
Sorry.

235
00:14:22,041 --> 00:14:23,945
They all turned us down.

236
00:14:24,777 --> 00:14:27,969
We really need to clear our names
of this allegation...

237
00:14:27,969 --> 00:14:33,361
So what should we do, Mr. Lawyer?

238
00:14:34,577 --> 00:14:37,949
Well, to deny copyright infringement...

239
00:14:37,949 --> 00:14:41,501
First, Tuesla is not similar to Hi, Ena.

240
00:14:41,501 --> 00:14:46,377
Second, Mr. Seo did not create Tuesla
by referencing Hi, Ena.

241
00:14:46,377 --> 00:14:49,421
You need to demonstrate one of
these two points to the other party.

242
00:14:49,421 --> 00:14:51,945
Neither Mr. Seo nor I
had ever seen Hi, Ena before.

243
00:14:51,945 --> 00:14:56,821
Proving that you hadn't seen it before
is actually extremely difficult.

244
00:14:56,821 --> 00:14:58,553
It's called the devil's proof.

245
00:14:58,553 --> 00:15:01,093
Devil, Demon Lord, I have no idea.

246
00:15:01,093 --> 00:15:05,297
But isn't it your job to do something
about that, Mr. Lawyer?

247
00:15:05,297 --> 00:15:09,877
Sorry. This is very, very difficult.

248
00:15:13,273 --> 00:15:15,513
Let's calm down.

249
00:15:15,513 --> 00:15:18,089
Wait a minute.

250
00:15:18,089 --> 00:15:19,957
What's this?

251
00:15:23,265 --> 00:15:24,265
[Savannah Central Banking Corporation]

252
00:15:24,265 --> 00:15:26,161
I showed people pictures of
both Tuesla and Hi, Ena,

253
00:15:26,161 --> 00:15:28,125
and asked if they were similar.

254
00:15:28,125 --> 00:15:30,561
I conducted a survey of 100 people.

255
00:15:30,561 --> 00:15:35,641
97 out of 100 people answered
that they are not similar.

256
00:15:35,641 --> 00:15:37,965
[Noritaka Yagi]

257
00:15:37,965 --> 00:15:39,800
So what?

258
00:15:40,713 --> 00:15:42,633
That's...

259
00:15:46,053 --> 00:15:48,857
I don't think that proves anything.

260
00:15:48,857 --> 00:15:50,733
That may be true.

261
00:15:50,733 --> 00:15:55,821
Denying similarity
in copyright issues is not easy.

262
00:15:55,821 --> 00:15:57,693
- By the way, Mr. Yagi...
- Yes?

263
00:15:57,693 --> 00:16:01,301
When did you first learn of
Tutu-Tuesla's existence?

264
00:16:01,301 --> 00:16:02,917
What? When?

265
00:16:02,917 --> 00:16:07,277
You came to our office
claiming it was a rip-off

266
00:16:07,277 --> 00:16:09,681
on the same day Tuesla was launched.

267
00:16:09,681 --> 00:16:13,021
But unfortunately, only one was sold.

268
00:16:13,021 --> 00:16:15,969
- Only one?
- Yes, only one.

269
00:16:15,969 --> 00:16:19,901
We thought we'd go all-in with plushies,
but reality was harsh.

270
00:16:19,901 --> 00:16:21,741
We tried promoting it on social media,

271
00:16:21,741 --> 00:16:24,313
but there was no reaction or sharing at all.

272
00:16:24,313 --> 00:16:25,777
What are you trying to say?

273
00:16:25,777 --> 00:16:28,253
In other words, at the time you showed up,

274
00:16:28,253 --> 00:16:31,633
Tuesla was barely known to the public.

275
00:16:32,345 --> 00:16:35,265
So it's strange.

276
00:16:35,265 --> 00:16:39,033
Where exactly did you learn of
Tuesla's existence?

277
00:16:40,269 --> 00:16:44,401
Well, you know, I mean, it was that...

278
00:16:44,401 --> 00:16:46,721
I can't seem to remember at all.

279
00:16:46,721 --> 00:16:50,441
Didn't you hear about Tuesla from someone?

280
00:16:50,441 --> 00:16:52,377
For example...

281
00:16:54,033 --> 00:16:55,897
this person, perhaps?

282
00:17:00,593 --> 00:17:04,333
I can't see it very clearly...
Well... Wait...

283
00:17:04,333 --> 00:17:06,466
My presbyopia has been getting worse lately.

284
00:17:07,097 --> 00:17:09,593
Can't you focus?

285
00:17:09,593 --> 00:17:13,789
Well, if you do happen to remember
where you first heard of Tuesla,

286
00:17:14,393 --> 00:17:17,166
please do let us know.

287
00:17:19,693 --> 00:17:21,401
Alright.

288
00:17:22,205 --> 00:17:24,553
- A photo?
- <i>Yes.</i>

289
00:17:24,553 --> 00:17:27,200
<i>Looks like it was taken secretly.</i>

290
00:17:27,200 --> 00:17:29,261
I see.

291
00:17:29,261 --> 00:17:32,517
<i>So there's a rat somewhere.</i>

292
00:17:32,517 --> 00:17:35,201
So... what will you do?

293
00:17:35,201 --> 00:17:37,825
We've already achieved
our objective sufficiently.

294
00:17:37,825 --> 00:17:39,829
I think we can pull out at this point.

295
00:17:39,829 --> 00:17:41,209
Understood.

296
00:17:41,209 --> 00:17:47,613
And, Mr. Omishima, what about our deal?

297
00:17:47,613 --> 00:17:49,437
<i>What do you mean?</i>

298
00:17:49,437 --> 00:17:52,373
I don't recall having such a conversation.

299
00:17:52,373 --> 00:17:53,929
Alright then, take care.

300
00:17:53,929 --> 00:17:55,217
Huh?

301
00:17:55,217 --> 00:17:57,377
Hey, wait! That's a problem for me!

302
00:17:57,377 --> 00:17:59,466
<i>Please excuse me.</i>

303
00:18:02,281 --> 00:18:06,066
Who could the rat be?

304
00:18:06,877 --> 00:18:09,566
Squeak, squeak.

305
00:18:18,005 --> 00:18:20,645
I see. Understood.

306
00:18:20,645 --> 00:18:23,045
Yes, alright.

307
00:18:24,597 --> 00:18:28,317
Savannah Central Bank is withdrawing
their rip-off allegation.

308
00:18:29,797 --> 00:18:33,025
They withdrew their allegation
right after being shown this photo...

309
00:18:33,025 --> 00:18:35,449
It means that the one pulling the strings
behind that Yagi guy

310
00:18:35,449 --> 00:18:37,377
was Mr. Omishima after all.

311
00:18:37,377 --> 00:18:39,965
That guy just keeps getting in our way.

312
00:18:39,965 --> 00:18:44,053
The rip-off allegation's been resolved,
so you can sell again.

313
00:18:45,637 --> 00:18:47,513
Thank you, Mugi.

314
00:18:47,513 --> 00:18:49,833
I'm glad, Anna.

315
00:18:55,265 --> 00:18:56,993
My grandma used to say that

316
00:18:56,993 --> 00:18:59,301
a guy who calls a woman
by her first name at work

317
00:18:59,301 --> 00:19:03,777
shouldn't be trusted, even if he is a lawyer.

318
00:19:03,777 --> 00:19:05,933
Huh? Then what should I call...

319
00:19:05,933 --> 00:19:07,767
Well, that's...

320
00:19:08,801 --> 00:19:12,033
Huh? Come to think of it,
I've never called her anything.

321
00:19:12,033 --> 00:19:15,893
Wait, you work together, and you've
never once called her by name?

322
00:19:15,893 --> 00:19:17,633
Nope, not once.

323
00:19:19,721 --> 00:19:22,425
I wonder who sent this?

324
00:19:22,425 --> 00:19:25,266
- This photo.
- That's impossible.

325
00:19:26,213 --> 00:19:30,837
- Wow!
- It hurts... It hurts.

326
00:19:30,837 --> 00:19:33,273
It hurts! Be a little gentler.

327
00:19:33,273 --> 00:19:35,566
Oh, that hurts! It hurts!

328
00:19:35,566 --> 00:19:38,305
Ah, this is bad! This is bad.

329
00:19:38,305 --> 00:19:41,000
I'm drooling. I'm drooling.

330
00:19:50,009 --> 00:19:51,566
What should I call her?

331
00:19:51,566 --> 00:19:55,881
Real name, Anna Kusakabe.
Occupation, consultant.

332
00:19:55,881 --> 00:19:58,133
O-Con? O-Con...

333
00:19:58,133 --> 00:20:01,773
Kusatchi? Kusamochi?

334
00:20:01,773 --> 00:20:05,866
Kabe... Kabe... Peki... Pekipeki.

335
00:20:06,693 --> 00:20:08,769
Nurikabe?

336
00:20:08,769 --> 00:20:10,997
How about that?

337
00:20:10,997 --> 00:20:15,293
Huh? Then I'll just drop the formalities
and call her by her first name.

338
00:20:15,293 --> 00:20:17,633
After all, I am her employer.

339
00:20:20,233 --> 00:20:21,889
An...

340
00:20:21,889 --> 00:20:24,833
An...

341
00:20:27,013 --> 00:20:28,921
Anna...

342
00:20:37,169 --> 00:20:39,193
Huh?

343
00:20:39,193 --> 00:20:41,001
That's scary!

344
00:20:43,349 --> 00:20:46,136
N-N-No. How is this...

345
00:20:48,157 --> 00:20:49,741
- Please, go ahead.
- Oh, sorry.

346
00:20:49,741 --> 00:20:52,753
You just can't help but sign up for
hometown tax donations,

347
00:20:52,753 --> 00:20:54,333
but then you can't eat
all the thank-you gifts.

348
00:20:54,333 --> 00:20:57,261
I know what you mean. That looks delicious.

349
00:20:57,261 --> 00:20:59,389
Yeah, this definitely goes well with sake.

350
00:20:59,389 --> 00:21:01,273
Right?

351
00:21:02,197 --> 00:21:03,861
The best!

352
00:21:03,861 --> 00:21:05,573
- The best! Right?
- Right.

353
00:21:05,573 --> 00:21:07,981
So, this is that photo.

354
00:21:07,981 --> 00:21:10,305
Wow! It's so small!

355
00:21:10,305 --> 00:21:14,200
At my age, I can't even see it. Huh?

356
00:21:15,517 --> 00:21:19,385
Huh? What's this? A topknot?

357
00:21:19,385 --> 00:21:21,169
A topknot?

358
00:21:32,017 --> 00:21:34,149
The person who sent this...

359
00:21:35,557 --> 00:21:37,533
was you, wasn't it?

360
00:21:39,549 --> 00:21:42,973
What are you saying? Why would I do that?

361
00:21:42,973 --> 00:21:44,700
In the photo.

362
00:21:45,569 --> 00:21:49,341
- You, Ms. Sasaoka.
- Me?

363
00:21:49,341 --> 00:21:53,700
Well, to be more precise,
it wasn't exactly you.

364
00:21:56,485 --> 00:21:58,233
It was Tuesla.

365
00:21:59,085 --> 00:22:02,669
At this point, the only person
to have bought Tuesla

366
00:22:02,669 --> 00:22:09,469
in the entire world is you,
Ms. Sasaoka. Only you.

367
00:22:12,065 --> 00:22:14,893
You worked fast. That was very helpful.

368
00:22:14,893 --> 00:22:17,493
I'm glad I could be of help.

369
00:22:17,493 --> 00:22:21,273
I'll proceed with the project as planned.

370
00:22:21,273 --> 00:22:23,129
Please do.

371
00:22:23,129 --> 00:22:25,293
Let's continue this good relationship.

372
00:22:25,293 --> 00:22:29,101
I feel like we can have a long relationship.

373
00:22:29,101 --> 00:22:30,461
Yes.

374
00:22:30,461 --> 00:22:32,886
Why did you send this email to me?

375
00:22:33,669 --> 00:22:38,617
There wasn't any deep meaning to it.

376
00:22:38,617 --> 00:22:41,200
Sorry, I have to go now.

377
00:22:47,301 --> 00:22:49,266
I'm back.

378
00:22:51,065 --> 00:22:54,165
I've been waiting, O-Con.

379
00:22:55,049 --> 00:22:56,277
What?

380
00:22:56,277 --> 00:23:01,300
After going full circle, starting today,
you are officially O-Con.

381
00:23:02,217 --> 00:23:05,700
Full circle? What circle did you go around?

382
00:23:07,021 --> 00:23:08,734
[Strategic Recovery and Growth Plan]
So the allegation of our character

383
00:23:08,734 --> 00:23:10,361
[for Plush Business]
being a rip-off has been resolved,

384
00:23:10,361 --> 00:23:12,245
and in thinking about how
to recover from here,

385
00:23:12,245 --> 00:23:14,133
I've come up with several plans.

386
00:23:15,565 --> 00:23:17,637
As for funds, we'll manage the royalties

387
00:23:17,637 --> 00:23:19,701
earned from "Cho-cho-cho-cho-cho-cho-cho,"

388
00:23:19,701 --> 00:23:22,113
the big hit in the Republic of Textorian.

389
00:23:22,113 --> 00:23:24,441
First, Plan A.

390
00:23:24,441 --> 00:23:27,177
[Create New Merchandise]
Start producing new Tuesla merchandise.

391
00:23:27,941 --> 00:23:29,385
[Plushie Advertising]
And Plan B.

392
00:23:29,385 --> 00:23:32,329
Allocate funds to advertising
for the existing plushies.

393
00:23:32,329 --> 00:23:36,677
So, which one does our consultant,
O-Con, recommend?

394
00:23:37,393 --> 00:23:40,189
As O-Con, I recommend Plan C.

395
00:23:40,189 --> 00:23:41,921
[Hire New Talent]

396
00:23:41,921 --> 00:23:46,765
With this money,
I recommend hiring new talent.

397
00:23:46,765 --> 00:23:48,085
New talent?

398
00:23:48,085 --> 00:23:50,873
After actually trying to sell Tuesla,
I realized that from here on out,

399
00:23:50,873 --> 00:23:52,991
we'll need someone
with extensive practical experience

400
00:23:52,991 --> 00:23:56,561
in the character business
and strong producing skills.

401
00:23:56,561 --> 00:23:58,725
I think we need someone like that.

402
00:23:58,725 --> 00:23:59,966
And not only that,

403
00:23:59,966 --> 00:24:03,505
but also someone who has a love
for characters and deep knowledge.

404
00:24:03,505 --> 00:24:05,085
For example,

405
00:24:05,085 --> 00:24:06,900
[Character Producer, Suzuka Sasaoka]
someone like Ms. Sasaoka.

406
00:24:08,129 --> 00:24:09,357
- What?
- No.

407
00:24:09,357 --> 00:24:12,565
- Ms. Sasaoka is certainly talented, but...
- No way.

408
00:24:12,565 --> 00:24:14,245
Absolutely not.

409
00:24:14,245 --> 00:24:16,749
- Just hypothetically speaking...
- Rejected!

410
00:24:16,749 --> 00:24:18,567
Rejection of rejections!

411
00:24:19,365 --> 00:24:21,165
Restroom.

412
00:24:25,209 --> 00:24:29,949
Mr. Seo and Ms. Sasaoka
were a really good duo.

413
00:24:29,949 --> 00:24:33,153
Like partners who could
bring out the best in each other.

414
00:24:33,153 --> 00:24:37,453
Then why are they now like
each other's mortal enemies?

415
00:24:37,453 --> 00:24:41,000
More like characters' enemies
than mortal enemies...

416
00:24:41,000 --> 00:24:42,900
Characters' enemies?

417
00:24:44,449 --> 00:24:47,262
Did you know that Full Tummy Molco

418
00:24:47,262 --> 00:24:50,377
was changed into Cynical Molco
by Mr. Omishima without permission?

419
00:24:50,377 --> 00:24:54,741
Yes, Mr. Seo said before
that he'd take vengeance.

420
00:24:54,741 --> 00:24:56,153
At that time,

421
00:24:56,153 --> 00:25:00,866
the one who changed it with Mr. Omishima
was Ms. Sasaoka.

422
00:25:01,809 --> 00:25:03,577
What?

423
00:25:04,289 --> 00:25:08,766
<i>So, I think it was a shock for Mr. Seo.</i>

424
00:25:18,389 --> 00:25:20,133
Ms. Sasaoka.

425
00:25:21,361 --> 00:25:23,193
The president is calling for you.

426
00:25:27,065 --> 00:25:29,245
So it was Ms. Sasaoka, right?

427
00:25:29,245 --> 00:25:34,481
The one who leaked my relationship
with Mr. Yagi of Savannah Central Bank.

428
00:25:35,641 --> 00:25:41,041
The purpose was to help Tuesla,
and by extension, Seo Design.

429
00:25:41,041 --> 00:25:47,433
Around me, there's only one person
I can think of who would do such a thing.

430
00:25:50,789 --> 00:25:52,665
That's right.

431
00:25:53,761 --> 00:25:55,709
I did it.

432
00:25:55,709 --> 00:25:57,805
I'm disappointed.

433
00:25:57,805 --> 00:26:01,466
To be betrayed by you,
someone whom I trusted.

434
00:26:03,761 --> 00:26:07,273
It's kind of like being bitten
by my own dog, isn't it?

435
00:26:07,273 --> 00:26:11,577
This is enough to make me
lose faith in people.

436
00:26:13,769 --> 00:26:19,633
But you've never trusted anyone
from the start, right?

437
00:26:24,229 --> 00:26:26,785
Am I fired?

438
00:26:26,785 --> 00:26:28,509
No way.

439
00:26:28,509 --> 00:26:32,749
You are a valuable asset to our company.
I won't fire you.

440
00:26:32,749 --> 00:26:35,033
But you will be...

441
00:26:35,637 --> 00:26:42,462
e-x-i-l-e-d. Death!

442
00:26:52,817 --> 00:26:57,266
Are you quitting, Ms. Sasaoka?

443
00:27:00,821 --> 00:27:02,533
No, I'm not quitting.

444
00:27:03,709 --> 00:27:08,365
But the place you're being transferred to...

445
00:27:08,365 --> 00:27:11,813
Wouldn't it be better to quit
than to go there?

446
00:27:11,813 --> 00:27:13,669
It's fine.

447
00:27:13,669 --> 00:27:16,400
It's a place that suits me.

448
00:27:22,989 --> 00:27:25,221
Isn't this great, this panel?

449
00:27:25,221 --> 00:27:27,349
You can understand
Tuesla's world at a glance.

450
00:27:27,349 --> 00:27:29,037
And it's also eye-catching.

451
00:27:29,037 --> 00:27:30,981
Right, Mr. Seo?

452
00:27:35,633 --> 00:27:41,217
Ah... Well, when I handle it,
it's a piece of cake.

453
00:27:46,749 --> 00:27:48,941
Huh?

454
00:27:48,941 --> 00:27:50,965
What's wrong?

455
00:27:50,965 --> 00:27:53,033
Ms. Sasaoka is...

456
00:28:00,213 --> 00:28:03,513
[Merry Co., Ltd. Reborn Center]

457
00:28:45,309 --> 00:28:47,769
She's fast. She's fast. She's fast!

458
00:28:47,769 --> 00:28:49,500
So fast!

459
00:29:11,525 --> 00:29:13,545
[Military Spirit Martial Arts Bar]

460
00:29:13,545 --> 00:29:15,700
A martial arts bar?

461
00:29:29,069 --> 00:29:31,233
I'll be coming here later. Nice to meet you.

462
00:29:31,233 --> 00:29:32,837
- Nice to meet you.
- Yo!

463
00:29:32,837 --> 00:29:34,773
Yo!

464
00:29:36,337 --> 00:29:38,173
Ms. Sasaoka.

465
00:29:41,737 --> 00:29:43,385
- Yo!
- Yo.

466
00:29:43,385 --> 00:29:45,217
Yo.

467
00:29:45,821 --> 00:29:49,373
So, why did you follow me?

468
00:29:50,733 --> 00:29:52,641
Well...

469
00:29:54,189 --> 00:29:56,433
I heard you got transferred.

470
00:29:57,841 --> 00:30:03,365
Because Mr. Omishima found out
that you sent us that photo...

471
00:30:03,365 --> 00:30:05,677
Is it right?

472
00:30:05,677 --> 00:30:08,733
Yes, he found out.

473
00:30:10,789 --> 00:30:14,817
- Isn't that retaliatory?
- It can't be helped.

474
00:30:14,817 --> 00:30:17,600
That's the kind of person Mr. Omishima is.

475
00:30:18,797 --> 00:30:22,033
Mr. Omishima is behind
the rip-off allegation.

476
00:30:22,853 --> 00:30:27,717
We only found out thanks to that photo.

477
00:30:27,717 --> 00:30:30,265
Thank you very much.

478
00:30:30,265 --> 00:30:31,869
Please don't.

479
00:30:31,869 --> 00:30:35,500
Because I've done something
that can't be atoned for with just this.

480
00:30:37,637 --> 00:30:39,689
Are you talking about...

481
00:30:40,309 --> 00:30:42,233
when you changed Full Tummy Molco?

482
00:30:57,845 --> 00:31:02,325
We'll take over the design of
Full Tummy Molco for now.

483
00:31:02,325 --> 00:31:04,129
What? But...

484
00:31:04,129 --> 00:31:07,425
You have other work
and are busy, right, Mr. Seo?

485
00:31:07,425 --> 00:31:09,369
It's almost finished.

486
00:31:09,369 --> 00:31:11,766
Ms. Sasaoka and I will do it.

487
00:31:15,941 --> 00:31:17,469
Alright, then.

488
00:31:17,469 --> 00:31:19,269
<i>Please take care of it.</i>

489
00:31:20,017 --> 00:31:23,666
[Cynical Molco]

490
00:31:23,666 --> 00:31:25,493
What is this?

491
00:31:25,493 --> 00:31:28,401
What the heck is this?
What happened to Full Tummy Molco?

492
00:31:30,309 --> 00:31:32,300
What's with this Cynical?

493
00:31:34,741 --> 00:31:37,557
It's only natural that I'm resented.

494
00:31:37,557 --> 00:31:40,100
I did something unforgivable.

495
00:31:41,745 --> 00:31:43,505
But...

496
00:31:44,341 --> 00:31:46,400
I can't believe it.

497
00:31:47,137 --> 00:31:49,773
That you would do something like that.

498
00:31:50,805 --> 00:31:52,577
What are you talking about?

499
00:31:53,365 --> 00:31:55,900
You don't know anything about me, do you?

500
00:31:58,909 --> 00:32:01,413
I do know.

501
00:32:02,365 --> 00:32:04,077
Huh?

502
00:32:04,077 --> 00:32:05,921
I do know.

503
00:32:07,653 --> 00:32:10,885
That you love the characters,

504
00:32:12,081 --> 00:32:14,897
<i>and that you love this job,</i>

505
00:32:14,897 --> 00:32:17,833
<i>and that you love what Mr. Seo creates.</i>

506
00:32:19,373 --> 00:32:24,100
I've finally come to understand
what it means to love something.

507
00:32:24,813 --> 00:32:29,389
So, when it comes to those
who love the same things,

508
00:32:29,389 --> 00:32:31,633
I know a comrade when I see one.

509
00:32:36,021 --> 00:32:37,900
What are you talking about?

510
00:32:38,681 --> 00:32:40,477
Weird.

511
00:32:42,553 --> 00:32:44,525
Ms. Sasaoka.

512
00:32:45,213 --> 00:32:48,213
Won't you lend us your strength for Tuesla?

513
00:32:49,521 --> 00:32:50,700
Huh?

514
00:32:50,700 --> 00:32:55,100
I'd feel reassured if you were with us.

515
00:32:57,329 --> 00:32:59,453
I can't.

516
00:32:59,453 --> 00:33:02,085
- But...
- This is my punishment.

517
00:33:03,733 --> 00:33:05,053
Punishment?

518
00:33:05,053 --> 00:33:07,657
Punishment for not being
able to protect Mr. Seo.

519
00:33:08,541 --> 00:33:10,457
It's karma.

520
00:33:18,037 --> 00:33:20,309
What did you just say?

521
00:33:20,309 --> 00:33:23,000
I said, I want to borrow Ms. Sasaoka's help.

522
00:33:23,609 --> 00:33:25,309
Rejection of rejections!

523
00:33:25,309 --> 00:33:26,941
That photo.

524
00:33:26,941 --> 00:33:29,533
The photo of Mr. Omishima and Mr. Yagi.

525
00:33:30,409 --> 00:33:35,333
The one who took that photo
and sent it to us was Ms. Sasaoka.

526
00:33:39,349 --> 00:33:44,121
To protect Seo Design, and to protect Tuesla.

527
00:33:47,573 --> 00:33:50,833
She said she did something that
can't be atoned for with just this.

528
00:33:52,621 --> 00:33:54,545
That's what she said.

529
00:34:01,425 --> 00:34:04,873
I'm going to step out for a bit.

530
00:34:07,097 --> 00:34:09,349
Please think about it.

531
00:34:09,349 --> 00:34:12,513
[13-2-21 Harumi, Chuo City, Tokyo,
Merry Reborn Center]

532
00:34:26,541 --> 00:34:29,541
So, what is it you wanted to discuss?

533
00:34:29,541 --> 00:34:33,000
And you even brought a lawyer, I see.

534
00:34:34,677 --> 00:34:38,393
We want you to stop your obstructive actions.

535
00:34:40,301 --> 00:34:43,821
How is this obstruction? I don't get it.

536
00:34:43,821 --> 00:34:48,045
Then, would it be alright
if we asked Mr. Yagi here in detail

537
00:34:48,045 --> 00:34:51,309
what you two talked about at that time?

538
00:34:51,309 --> 00:34:53,417
If you're also pressed,

539
00:34:53,417 --> 00:34:56,033
there are plenty of things
that could go badly for you, right?

540
00:34:56,693 --> 00:34:59,565
If you try anything further,

541
00:34:59,565 --> 00:35:02,569
we will take our own measures
to defend ourselves.

542
00:35:02,569 --> 00:35:04,329
Is that clear?

543
00:35:33,749 --> 00:35:36,613
Did you hear about this from Ms. Kusakabe?

544
00:35:36,613 --> 00:35:38,733
That I'm here.

545
00:35:41,869 --> 00:35:44,266
Are you thinking, "Serves you right"?

546
00:35:47,049 --> 00:35:48,900
Why did you change it?

547
00:35:50,013 --> 00:35:52,033
We made it together.

548
00:35:52,985 --> 00:35:55,233
Why didn't you protect
Full Tummy Molco back then?

549
00:35:55,233 --> 00:35:58,133
I wanted to protect it too!

550
00:36:00,353 --> 00:36:02,133
I wanted to protect it too.

551
00:36:03,997 --> 00:36:05,797
W-W-Wait a minute.

552
00:36:05,797 --> 00:36:08,273
You changed it without permission?

553
00:36:08,273 --> 00:36:09,817
But you can't do that.

554
00:36:09,817 --> 00:36:11,449
This is Mr. Seo's...

555
00:36:11,449 --> 00:36:15,783
- That's why I removed him.
- But...

556
00:36:15,783 --> 00:36:19,977
Designers who can't obey me,
the company representative,

557
00:36:19,977 --> 00:36:24,966
will have to be erased
along with their characters.

558
00:36:27,233 --> 00:36:29,381
<i>If I don't listen to the president,</i>

559
00:36:29,381 --> 00:36:32,921
then you, Mr. Seo,
and the characters you create,

560
00:36:32,921 --> 00:36:34,929
you will all be made to have never existed.

561
00:36:34,929 --> 00:36:36,849
That's why...

562
00:36:38,017 --> 00:36:40,117
Why didn't you say so?

563
00:36:41,933 --> 00:36:44,500
How could I possibly say it?

564
00:36:46,981 --> 00:36:51,901
No matter how I tried to cover it up,
I was complicit with the president.

565
00:36:52,781 --> 00:36:58,745
But in the end, you quit the company,
and Molco became Cynical Molco.

566
00:36:58,745 --> 00:37:01,705
Because of the president,
the company got weirder and weirder.

567
00:37:01,705 --> 00:37:03,466
Then you should have quit.

568
00:37:04,661 --> 00:37:10,897
If I'd quit, then the characters you created,

569
00:37:10,897 --> 00:37:13,166
I wouldn't have been able to
protect them, right?

570
00:37:15,200 --> 00:37:17,849
To protect them from that president,

571
00:37:17,849 --> 00:37:20,941
I had to stay in the company
and keep an eye on things.

572
00:37:21,725 --> 00:37:24,245
No matter what kind of place it is,

573
00:37:24,245 --> 00:37:29,166
as long as I stayed in the company,
I figured I could manage somehow.

574
00:37:32,765 --> 00:37:37,733
I did something to you that's unforgivable.

575
00:37:40,261 --> 00:37:42,033
So...

576
00:37:44,213 --> 00:37:46,866
this is the only thing I can do.

577
00:38:08,893 --> 00:38:10,866
An opening!

578
00:38:22,453 --> 00:38:25,545
Sorry, sorry. I did that without thinking.

579
00:38:25,545 --> 00:38:27,866
Well, are you okay?

580
00:38:29,429 --> 00:38:31,466
Sure-Kill! Return Strike!

581
00:38:38,777 --> 00:38:43,325
That makes us even!

582
00:38:43,325 --> 00:38:44,925
Huh?

583
00:38:44,925 --> 00:38:49,400
That thing! Go side! Go side!

584
00:38:50,169 --> 00:38:51,449
Huh?

585
00:38:51,449 --> 00:38:53,777
In rugby, you know,

586
00:38:53,777 --> 00:38:57,253
once the game is over,
there are no hard feelings.

587
00:38:57,253 --> 00:38:59,089
Go side!

588
00:39:00,365 --> 00:39:02,149
It should be "no side".

589
00:39:02,865 --> 00:39:07,581
With this, this matter is settled.
No more hard feelings.

590
00:39:07,581 --> 00:39:09,289
Alright?

591
00:39:10,881 --> 00:39:12,709
Alright.

592
00:39:17,585 --> 00:39:20,989
I bet O-Con will be surprised.

593
00:39:20,989 --> 00:39:23,809
"As expected of Mr. Seo! Wonderful! Hehe..."

594
00:39:23,809 --> 00:39:26,041
I bet she'll say something like that.

595
00:39:36,817 --> 00:39:39,141
[Resignation Letter: Suzuka Sasaoka]

596
00:39:51,269 --> 00:39:53,493
Thank you so much, Mugi.

597
00:39:55,117 --> 00:39:59,233
You were cool as a lawyer.

598
00:39:59,989 --> 00:40:01,333
Thank you.

599
00:40:01,333 --> 00:40:04,617
What's that guy doing at
someone else's house...

600
00:40:04,617 --> 00:40:08,366
I'm glad my last job as a lawyer
was for you, Anna.

601
00:40:09,289 --> 00:40:11,329
Huh? Your last job?

602
00:40:11,329 --> 00:40:13,189
Yeah.

603
00:40:13,189 --> 00:40:15,201
I'm not going to be a lawyer anymore.

604
00:40:15,201 --> 00:40:17,117
Why?

605
00:40:17,117 --> 00:40:18,585
What do you mean?

606
00:40:18,585 --> 00:40:20,817
Could it be that
your girlfriend said something?

607
00:40:20,817 --> 00:40:22,973
Are you really that henpecked?

608
00:40:23,941 --> 00:40:26,321
Girlfriend?

609
00:40:26,321 --> 00:40:29,433
Oh, no, no! Meru isn't my girlfriend.

610
00:40:29,433 --> 00:40:32,200
But you said that
you've met someone you like.

611
00:40:32,200 --> 00:40:34,366
The person I fell in love with...

612
00:40:35,325 --> 00:40:37,125
are they.

613
00:40:37,125 --> 00:40:39,145
Arnold and Sylvester.

614
00:40:40,297 --> 00:40:42,177
Huh?

615
00:40:43,405 --> 00:40:46,613
The moment we met, I fell in love...

616
00:40:46,613 --> 00:40:48,601
with those muscles!

617
00:40:50,173 --> 00:40:54,337
I want to become a muscle idol
together with them,

618
00:40:54,337 --> 00:40:56,405
<i>so I begged their manager, Meru,</i>

619
00:40:56,405 --> 00:40:59,585
<i>saying I'd even carry bags or do anything.</i>

620
00:40:59,585 --> 00:41:01,517
If you put it that way,

621
00:41:02,285 --> 00:41:05,381
want to become my disciple-muscle?

622
00:41:05,381 --> 00:41:07,581
Please let me be your disciple, muscle!

623
00:41:07,581 --> 00:41:11,193
I somehow managed to become his disciple.

624
00:41:11,193 --> 00:41:12,813
Disciple.

625
00:41:12,813 --> 00:41:16,000
I want to devote everything to this love.

626
00:41:17,449 --> 00:41:21,733
And besides... idols shouldn't have lovers...

627
00:41:22,385 --> 00:41:24,300
So, well...

628
00:41:25,169 --> 00:41:27,265
I'm sorry.

629
00:41:27,265 --> 00:41:30,613
I ended up hurting you.

630
00:41:30,613 --> 00:41:33,193
I'm really sorry!

631
00:41:38,749 --> 00:41:40,969
I understand.

632
00:41:40,969 --> 00:41:42,669
Now, I really do.

633
00:41:46,037 --> 00:41:48,866
That feeling of "love".

634
00:41:55,261 --> 00:41:58,233
And the feeling of wanting to
devote everything.

635
00:42:04,669 --> 00:42:06,493
I understand now.

636
00:42:07,441 --> 00:42:09,189
Anna.

637
00:42:12,257 --> 00:42:14,317
Mugi.

638
00:42:14,317 --> 00:42:16,466
Thank you so much for everything.

639
00:42:19,325 --> 00:42:21,217
Your dream of becoming an idol,

640
00:42:22,301 --> 00:42:24,253
make it come true, okay?

641
00:42:24,873 --> 00:42:28,673
Thank you, Anna.

642
00:42:30,357 --> 00:42:34,566
Lastly, could you listen to one song for me?

643
00:42:35,285 --> 00:42:36,429
Huh?

644
00:42:36,429 --> 00:42:39,700
Yeah, let me hear it.

645
00:42:42,789 --> 00:42:44,761
Alright, then please listen to

646
00:42:45,369 --> 00:42:50,609
Arnold and Sylvester's Muscle Lovers.

647
00:42:50,609 --> 00:42:55,565
[Muscle Lovers by Arnold and Sylvester]

648
00:42:58,589 --> 00:43:05,509
<i>♪ One day I was struck by lightning ♪</i>

649
00:43:05,509 --> 00:43:12,733
<i>♪ This thrilling spark that came tingling ♪</i>

650
00:43:12,733 --> 00:43:19,465
<i>♪ Yes, this isn't static electricity ♪</i>

651
00:43:19,465 --> 00:43:27,465
<i>♪ It's love. It was the beginning of love ♪</i>

652
00:43:28,777 --> 00:43:35,485
<i>♪ One day, my eyes met yours ♪</i>

653
00:43:35,485 --> 00:43:42,933
<i>♪ This thrill I want to gaze at forever ♪</i>

654
00:43:42,933 --> 00:43:50,069
- <i>♪ Yes, this pain in my chest ♪</i>
- <i>♪ This pain ♪</i>

655
00:43:50,069 --> 00:43:56,813
<i>♪ No, it's not intercostal neuralgia ♪</i>

656
00:43:56,813 --> 00:44:03,909
<i>♪ It's love, the pain of love ♪</i>

657
00:44:03,909 --> 00:44:11,909
<i>♪ It's love. It was muscle pain ♪</i>

658
00:44:14,989 --> 00:44:22,053
- <i>♪ Wherever I am, I think of you ♪</i>
- <i>♪ Of muscles ♪</i>

659
00:44:22,053 --> 00:44:26,545
- <i>♪ Love, this is love, this is love ♪</i>
- Come on!

660
00:44:26,545 --> 00:44:34,857
<i>♪ Love, love, love... ♪</i>

661
00:44:44,233 --> 00:44:46,089
So this is...

662
00:44:47,137 --> 00:44:48,845
love.
